1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:03,430
A forklift strikes a
worker on the night shift.

2
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:06,660
Everyone asks the same
question: why did it happen?

3
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:09,460
Start with the events,
in order, to the second:

4
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:12,390
the forklift into the aisle,
the picker crossing its end,

5
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:13,829
the reverse out.

6
00:00:14,129 --> 00:00:17,159
Then the conditions that held
at the time: a ten-hour night,

7
00:00:17,209 --> 00:00:21,019
the light at the aisle end out
since Tuesday, no spotter.

8
00:00:21,069 --> 00:00:23,188
All of them still there at the collision.

9
00:00:23,538 --> 00:00:27,098
Link each one to what it led to,
and you mark the causal factors,

10
00:00:27,148 --> 00:00:31,816
and the root cause behind them: nobody
reviewed the risks of the longer shifts.

11
00:00:32,116 --> 00:00:35,506
OpenChronology keeps the whole
chain on one exact timeline,

12
00:00:35,556 --> 00:00:37,287
for everyone checking it.

13
00:00:37,627 --> 00:00:41,309
Events, conditions, causes. It's free.
